 of the competition but the medals were to be decided exclusively by the scores in the Briton’s speciality, the final Grand Prix Freestyle to music section. Dujardin scored within a percentage point of her own world record to become the first British woman ever to retain an individual Olympic title and briefly become Great Britain’s most successful female Olympian before " [:a {:href "/athletes/124053"} "Laura Trott"] "’s subsequent wins. Werth’s silver was her 10th medal in an Olympic career that began in 1992 and she was joined in the medal positions by her compatriot " [:a {:href "/athletes/125643"} "Kristina Bröring-Sprehe"] ". Another German-born rider, " [:a {:href "/athletes/135450"} "Christian Zimmermann"] ", became the first ever Olympic equestrian to represent Palestine while Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/128984"} "Sue Hearn"] " was a débutant at the age of 60."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Grand Prix"] [:th {} "Grand Prix Special"] [:th {} "Grand Prix Kür Freestyle"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "230"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125495"} "Charlotte Dujardin"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/3427"} "Valegro"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "85.071 (1)"] [:td {} "82.983 (2)"] [:td {} "93.857 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "237"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11503"} "Isabell Werth"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/3829"} "Weihegold Old"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/G